<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Monex returns to profit, pays arrears div.</title>
<headline>Monex returns to profit, pays arrears div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		34.4	  vs loss 12.3</p>
<p>    - attrib		  34.8	  vs loss 13.2</p>
<p>    Net profit		11.39	 vs loss 3.07</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   17.94	 vs loss 4.42</p>
<p>    Tax paid		   3.77	 vs gain 1.36</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    2.02	 vs 1.55</p>
<p>    Turnover		  66.65	 vs 23.98</p>
<p>Full name: Monex Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The property development group said that its return to profitability had enabled it to declare and pay the arrears final dividend of 2.77 million rand on cumulative redeemable preference shares on April 11.</p>
<p>The return to profitability after two years of losses provided a solid foundation for the future. Efforts to realise the potential of its Century City development outside Cape Town should begin to bear fruit in the second half of the year to March 1998 with meaningful returns likely in the year to March 1999 and beyond, it said.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
